        "short_description": "Placeholder for a national professional ice hockey league: 32 teams in two conferences of two divisions (eight teams each), an 82-game regular season, a 16-team divisional playoff bracket of best-of-seven series. Onboarding renames this and every Team N."
      },
      "lore": [
        {
          "title": "Structure",
          "content": "Conference A has Division North and Division East; Conference B has Division Central and Division West; eight teams per division. Each season the team's COMPETES_IN edge carries conference (\"Conference A\") and group (the division alone, \"Division North\"); the team's standing conference and division are also tags (conference-a, division-north). Rename the competition, the conferences and divisions, and the teams (full name, short_name, abbreviation, city) to what the owner's league uses; the tags can stay. Vocabulary: rule/sport_ice_hockey; game-night routine: rule/ice_hockey_game_log. Standings use the 2-1-0 loser-point system with regulation wins as the first tiebreaker after points percentage.",
          "display_index": 0
        }
      ]
